  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Louisiana total $5.1B in FY2026 to date. Louisiana has 21,769 awards so far, with an average award size of $234K, and obligations are up 7.0% year over year. Obligations have varied across recent fiscal years: FY21 was $4B, FY22 was $3.7B, FY23 was $4.5B, FY24 was $3.9B, and FY25 was $4.8B. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Defense are the two largest buyers in the state. Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry by obligations, and a small set of vendors account for a large share of spending. This snapshot is based on contract obligations and reflects fiscal year to date totals, so current-year totals are partial. Contractors and procurement teams should note concentration by agency, industry, and vendor when planning pursuits or partnerships. The data shows where federal dollars are currently concentrated and which firms and sectors are winning the largest obligations in Louisiana.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal spending in Louisiana?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.5B. Department of Defense obligated $1.8B. Department of Energy obligated $264M, and remaining top buyers include Department of Agriculture at $102M and Department of Veterans Affairs at $85.7M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors capture the most obligations in Louisiana?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $2.7B in obligations. Other large industries include Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $476M and Facilities Support Services at $417M. BOLLINGER SHIPYARDS LOCKPORT, L.L.C. received $2.3B, followed by STRATEGIC STORAGE PARTNERS, LLC. at $430M and PITTMAN-SEALEVEL, L.L.C. at $420M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Louisiana?",
      "a": "Louisiana receives $5.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state has 21,769 awards so far, with an average award size of $234K, and obligations are up 7.0% year over year. Recent fiscal-year totals include FY21 at $4B, FY22 at $3.7B, FY23 at $4.5B, FY24 at $3.9B, and FY25 at $4.8B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Louisiana?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, having obligated $2.5B. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer with $1.8B, followed by the Department of Energy at $264M, the Department of Agriculture at $102M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $85.7M."
    },
